{"ts": "2026-06-24T08:33:27Z", "event_kind": "provider_agent_session", "summary": "openai/gpt-4o-mini sess=sess_fa2 turns=1 cost=$0.0002", "payload": {"session_id": "sess_fa2fc864563c", "ts_start": "2026-06-24T08:33:24Z", "ts_end": "2026-06-24T08:33:27Z", "provider": "openai", "model": "gpt-4o-mini", "task": "# QSB Trading \u2014 Find the Winning Equation\n\n## Current state (REAL trades, last 90min)\n- 53 traders + 26 ensembles on OANDA practice + Alpaca paper + Binance testnet\n- Pot: \u00a35000 cap, atomic reserve/release working\n- Total real PnL: -\u00a311.36 (last 1h on dashboard)\n- 58.6% wr overall\n\n## What we tried (all failed to flip positive sustainably)\n1. Per-instrument stop multipliers (EUR/GBP 0.8x) \u2014 fixed early bleed\n2. Kelly sizing (winners 1-2\u00d7, losers 0.1\u00d7) \u2014 worked when wr stable\n3. Vol-adjusted stops by venue (binance 2.5\u21921.8x) \u2014 fixed bnbusdt asymmetry\n4. Hard absolute \u00a3-cap per trade (5\u21924\u21922.50) \u2014 losses STILL slip \u00a30.30-\u00a30.80 past\n5. Shrink JPY position 500\u2192300 \u2192 restore 500 \u2014 neutral\n6. Decouple profit_take from stop_mult (1.5\u03c3 flat) \u2014 wins reach further BUT\n   - JPY still hit 2 losses of -\u00a33.28 and -\u00a32.74 in 1min after fix\n\n## Asymmetric exit signature\nJPY: 60% wr / avg win \u00a31.51 / avg loss \u00a33.69 (loss 2.4\u00d7 larger)\n- Wins exit at profit_lock / profit_take (~0.5-1\u03c3)\n- Losses exit at abs_stop_2.50 + slip to \u00a32.70-\u00a33.30\n- Slip happens because abs_stop fires when next tick crosses trigger;\n  during the tick gap, price keeps moving against us.\n\n## What I see\nThe \"trigger fires \u2192 next-tick fill\" model bleeds in fast markets.\nNeed PRE-EMPTIVE exit or TRAILING that locks at the peak, not absolute.\n\n## ASK \u2014 design the winning equation\n\nONE of these approaches (or combine) \u2014 pick what you'd bet on:\nA. TRAILING STOP \u2014 track unrealized peak; exit when retraces N% of peak.\n   No fixed \u00a3 cap. Locks each move's profit, not absolute level.\n\nB. KELLY-BANDIT \u2014 start each instrument at 1/N units. After 30 closes,\n   re-weight by Sharpe (mean/std of pnl). Instruments with neg Sharpe go\n   to 0 size. Auto-pause without flag.\n\nC. ENSEMBLE-ONLY \u2014 disable all single-strategy traders. Only run ensembles\n   (require \u22652 of 3 strategies agree). Higher entry bar = fewer trades,\n   higher wr.\n\nD. REGIME GATE \u2014 only OPEN when belief.regime_confidence > 0.8 AND\n   ticks_since_last_loss > 10. Refuses entry in choppy state. Less volume,\n   higher quality.\n\nE. ANTI-MARTINGALE \u2014 double size after a win, reset after a loss.\n   Capitalizes on winning streaks while losses stay small.\n\nF. (your design) \u2014 propose new equation.\n\nReply: ONE letter + 3 sentences of why + the specific math/threshold.", "turns": 1, "total_cost_usd": 0.000199, "tool_calls": [], "final_text": "A. TRAILING STOP \u2014 This approach allows for locking in profits by tracking the unrealized peak, which can help mitigate losses during fast market movements. By exiting when the price retraces a certain percentage of the peak, it adapts to market volatility and reduces the impact of slippage. I propose a trailing stop that exits when the price retraces 2% from the peak.\n\nMath/Threshold: Exit when current price \u2264 (peak price - (peak price * 0.02))."}}
